{"type":"MarkdownJsnodeOperationPackageFabricationReceipt","version":1,"sourceDigest":"sha256:56fabb993b5d3a509e5909c76cfc04186c9da473efda999e189e938630691c58","specificationDigest":"sha256:ecfabecae8bc101a7085bb2689f4558d0858beca4902f92741f72b3edbf3cf26","artifactSpecification":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSpecification","version":1,"source":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSource","version":1,"identity":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceIdentity","id":"derive-set-of-duplication-work-intents"},"provenance":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceProvenance","locator":"/home/emsenn/info/lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/engineering-services-section/services/computer-engineering-services-section/services/computer-code-services-section/services/javascript-services-section/services/javascript-node-services-section/services/jsnode-workspace-analysis-services-section/content/text/documents/specifications/derive-set-of-duplication-work-intents-work-order.md","digest":"sha256:56fabb993b5d3a509e5909c76cfc04186c9da473efda999e189e938630691c58","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":1,"endLine":269}}},"artifact":{"type":"FabricatedArtifactIdentity","version":1,"id":"derive-set-of-duplication-work-intents","kind":"jsnode-operation-package"},"requirements":[{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"cross-package-only","statement":"The operation considers only cross-package candidates: a candidate whose `packages` array carries fewer than two entries is skipped and counted in `skippedSinglePackage` rather than turned into an intent.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":3,"endLine":3}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"one-intent-per-candidate","statement":"The operation returns a `DuplicationWorkIntentSet` (`type`, `version: 1`, `derivedAt`, `considered`, `skippedSinglePackage`, `intents`) with exactly one `metroplat.work.structured-intent` in `intents` per remaining cross-package candidate, up to `request.limit` (default 25); `considered` is the total candidates given, regardless of the limit.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":4,"endLine":4}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"chain-carried-verbatim","statement":"Every intent's `items` array opens with the four given `chain` items (endeavor, campaign, project, plan), each carried into a structured item verbatim (`cell`, `parent` when given, `text` unchanged) with the operation's own synthesized `evidence`/`provenance` added so each item satisfies `structured-work-intent-admit`'s item shape.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":5,"endLine":5}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"one-task-per-intent","statement":"Each intent's `items` array closes with one task item whose `cell` is `task:migrate-consumer-<fingerprint-prefix>` (the candidate's `semanticFingerprint`, first 12 characters), parented to the given chain's plan cell, stating the copied function's name, the packages it is copied in, and its consumer count.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":6,"endLine":6}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"refusal-first-step","statement":"When a `jsnode.duplication-migration.plan` exists for the candidate (looked up by `candidate.semanticFingerprint` against `plans[].candidate.semanticFingerprint`), its `refusals` appear verbatim as the task's first step; an `owner-republish-required` refusal is rendered as \"publish `<owner>` exporting `<name>`, then apply the plan\" naming the plan's own `owner` and `ownerExport.name`.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":7,"endLine":7}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"no-plan-no-owner-step","statement":"When no plan exists and the candidate carries no `existingUpstreamOwner`, the task's first step names \"no owner: seat one in the section that owns the primitive\" instead of a publish step.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":8,"endLine":8}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"horizon-by-consumer-count","statement":"Every task carries modality MUST, force `necessary`, and horizon `soon`, except a candidate with 8 or more consumers, whose horizon is `now`; all three are stated in the task's own text (`modality=... force=... horizon=...`), following the precedent set by the 2026-09-04 owner-finance-asks-intent's embedded `force=... modality=... horizon=...` items.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":9,"endLine":9}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"gate-stated-per-task","statement":"Every task's text closes with its gate: \"the plan applies (`jsnode-computer duplication-migration --apply`), the consumers' tests pass, the owner is published, and `jsnode_duplication` no longer lists `<fingerprint-prefix>`\".","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":10,"endLine":10}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationRequirement","version":1,"id":"pure-derivation","statement":"The operation performs no filesystem or network access; it transforms only the `candidates`, `plans`, `chain`, and optional `derivedAt` it is given, defaulting `derivedAt` to its own wall clock when omitted so a caller can pass a fixed value for deterministic examples and tests. Admission is a separate script's job — this operation admits nothing itself.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":11,"endLine":11}}],"prohibitions":[{"type":"ArtifactFabricationProhibition","version":1,"id":"candidates-must-be-array","statement":"The operation must refuse (throw `TypeError`) a request whose `candidates` is not an array.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":13,"endLine":13}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationProhibition","version":1,"id":"chain-must-be-four-items","statement":"The operation must refuse a request whose `chain` is not an array of exactly four items.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":14,"endLine":14}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationProhibition","version":1,"id":"plan-must-carry-fingerprint","statement":"The operation must refuse a request carrying a `plans` entry whose `candidate.semanticFingerprint` is missing or empty.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":15,"endLine":15}}],"openQuestions":[],"constraints":[{"type":"ArtifactFabricationConstraint","version":1,"id":"admitted-example-face-equivalence","kind":"law","authority":"JSNode operation face-equivalence law","revision":"v1","locator":"lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/engineering-services-section/services/computer-engineering-services-section/services/computer-code-engineering-services-section/services/javascript-engineering-services-section/services/javascript-code-fabrication-services-section/services/javascript-node-code-fabrication-services-section/services/jsnode-package-services-section/README.md","applicability":"Applies to the shared example projected to the JSNode import and command faces.","statement":"Every admitted example has equivalent import and command outputs under the downstream JSNode face assay.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":17,"endLine":17}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationConstraint","version":1,"id":"primitives-exist-once","kind":"law","authority":"561 Group working discipline","revision":"2026-08-30","locator":"CLAUDE.md","applicability":"Applies to every candidate this operation turns into a migrate-consumer duty.","statement":"Primitives exist once, on the registry, interdependent — never copied; a rendered duty is one more copy this operation dispatches toward retirement.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":18,"endLine":18}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationConstraint","version":1,"id":"platform-dispatches-consolidation","kind":"law","authority":"Founder ruling, 2026-09-05","revision":"v1","locator":"this specification's own founding order","applicability":"Applies to the whole operation's reason for existing.","statement":"\"you generalized the code; you never cut over consumers\"; \"the YouTube channels should get automatically refabricated\" — consolidation is dispatched by the platform as duties on the work rail, never left to a session's own reading of the duplication graph.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":19,"endLine":19}},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationConstraint","version":1,"id":"node-esm-operation","kind":"standard","authority":"Node.js","revision":"v24.2.0+","locator":"https://nodejs.org/docs/v24/api/esm.html","applicability":"Applies to the .mjs operation, its import.meta.main guard, and downstream package-birth assays.","statement":"The package uses one executable ESM operation source file that is eligible for downstream staged package-birth assays.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":21,"endLine":21}}],"projections":[{"type":"ArtifactFabricationProjection","version":1,"id":"jsnode-operation-package","target":"@red-cup-engineering/jsnode-operation-package-specification-admission-service","configuration":{"type":"JsnodeOperationPackageSpecificationCandidate","version":1,"packageName":"@red-cup-engineering/derive-set-of-duplication-work-intents-service","packageVersion":"0.1.0","license":"MIT","dependencies":{},"devDependencies":{}},"sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":25,"endLine":256}}],"acceptanceObligations":[{"type":"ArtifactFabricationAcceptanceObligation","version":1,"id":"jsnode-package-assays","kind":"assay","statement":"The existing JSNode package-birth pipeline must admit, stage, test, pack, install, and assay the projected package.","sourceSpan":{"type":"ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan","startLine":168,"endLine":256}}],"traceability":[{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"cross-package-only","constraintIds":["node-esm-operation","primitives-exist-once"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"one-intent-per-candidate","constraintIds":["node-esm-operation","platform-dispatches-consolidation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"chain-carried-verbatim","constraintIds":["admitted-example-face-equivalence"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"one-task-per-intent","constraintIds":["platform-dispatches-consolidation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"refusal-first-step","constraintIds":["platform-dispatches-consolidation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"no-plan-no-owner-step","constraintIds":["primitives-exist-once"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"horizon-by-consumer-count","constraintIds":["platform-dispatches-consolidation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"gate-stated-per-task","constraintIds":["platform-dispatches-consolidation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"pure-derivation","constraintIds":["node-esm-operation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"candidates-must-be-array","constraintIds":["admitted-example-face-equivalence","node-esm-operation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"chain-must-be-four-items","constraintIds":["admitted-example-face-equivalence","node-esm-operation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]},{"type":"ArtifactFabricationTrace","version":1,"requirementId":"plan-must-carry-fingerprint","constraintIds":["admitted-example-face-equivalence","node-esm-operation"],"projectionIds":["jsnode-operation-package"],"acceptanceObligationIds":["jsnode-package-assays"]}],"specificationDigest":"sha256:ecfabecae8bc101a7085bb2689f4558d0858beca4902f92741f72b3edbf3cf26"},"jsnodeOperationPackageCreationReceipt":{"type":"JsnodeOperationPackageCreationReceipt","version":1,"packageName":"@red-cup-engineering/derive-set-of-duplication-work-intents-service","packageVersion":"0.1.0","destination":"/home/emsenn/info/lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/engineering-services-section/services/computer-engineering-services-section/services/computer-code-services-section/services/javascript-services-section/services/javascript-node-services-section/services/jsnode-workspace-analysis-services-section/services/derive-set-of-duplication-work-intents-service","filesDigest":"sha256:36edf5e66926d600279e1bdc9d43900f091befd5a3ed79cacb36281e21dc924e","files":[{"type":"TextFileMaterialization","version":1,"path":"package.json","mode":420,"digest":"sha256:24b6f3f608d8a468f069f44d535d28caa847d16381f0db62651ad486cb0fb262"},{"type":"TextFileMaterialization","version":1,"path":"README.md","mode":420,"digest":"sha256:0a5f4362395a97b0c8021fa960dbacf2b7b689d49a86d2ccb918296871d614e3"},{"type":"TextFileMaterializ